// Pull request author: Sh4dow-BR
// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: Suspicious WSL Binary Hijack via Proxy Execution
// Sigma ID: 88d306e9-8e2d-4025-9768-28757d2732db
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-05-05 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1036.005, T1218
// Description: Detects C:\Windows\System32\wsl.exe spawning a child wsl.exe process from outside the legitimate
//   WSL install locations. When WSL or bash is invoked, the System32 stub (wsl.exe) looks up the
//   InstallLocation registry key and executes the wsl.exe found there. An attacker who modifies
//   InstallLocation to a controlled path causes the stub to transparently proxy execution to a
//   malicious payload, which then appears as a wsl.exe child of the legitimate System32 stub.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20260718025639/https://cardinalops.com/blog/bash-and-switch-hijacking-via-windows-subsystem-for-linux/
//   - https://blog.qualys.com/vulnerabilities-threat-research/2022/04/20/implications-of-windows-subsystem-for-linux-for-adversaries-defenders-part-2
//   - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/new-malware-uses-windows-subsystem-for-linux-for-stealthy-attacks/
//   - https://thehackernews.com/2021/09/new-malware-targets-windows-subsystem.html
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/3b26628c02b9f77741b6f068e9ce40a87740d455/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_wsl_binary_hijack_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\System32\\wsl.exe" and FolderPath endswith "\\wsl.exe") and (not(((FolderPath in~ ("C:\\Windows\\System32\\wsl.exe", "C:\\Program Files\\WSL\\wsl.exe")) or (FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\WinSxS\\amd64_microsoft-windows-lxss-wsl_" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\WinSxS\\arm64_microsoft-windows-lxss-wsl_" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\WindowsApps\\MicrosoftCorporationII.WindowsSubsystemForLinux") or (FolderPath startswith "C:\\Users\\" and FolderPath contains "\\AppData\\Local\\Microsoft\\WindowsApps\\"))))
